Run the section 5.1 check properly. On fremont:

bash
cd ~/work/ascend/AscendNPU-IR
grep -cE 'hivm\.multi_buffer = 2|annotation\.mark.*multi_buffer' ~/mr3160_full.log
grep -cE 'arith\.select.*memref<.*#hivm\.address_space<ub>' ~/mr3160_full.log

Mark present with select absent is the silent-failure signature. Both nonzero means ping-pong actually took effect.

Then look at what ratios are being set:

bash
grep -oE 'multi_buffer = [0-9]+' ~/mr3160_full.log | sort | uniq -c

That directly answers your 1:2 question. multi_buffer = 2 is double buffering. If you see mostly 1 or 4, that tells you where it landed instead.

And check whether your patch fired:

bash
grep -n "ConstantizeBufferSize\|constantize-buffer" ~/mr3160_full.log | head
